I am unable to parse this as a valid response. It appears to be a series of typos or errors rather than a proper response. I will need to generate a new response based on the given news and questions.

[news information]
Title: Kiwoom Securities, Enhancing IB Capability through SPAC Merger... Aiming for Large-scale IB]
Text: Kiwoom Securities is pushing forward three consecutive SPAC (Special Purpose Acquisition Company) mergers at the beginning of the year, accelerating its IB (Investment Banking) business capabilities. This is interpreted as a move to diversify its business portfolio which was previously centered on retail, as it aims to enter the large-scale IB market by the end of the year.

On August 8th, according to the investment banking industry, Kiwoom Securities is currently promoting the 6th to 8th SPAC mergers. The 6th Kiwoom SPAC is merging with Ercos, a food tech company. The 7th is planned to merge with Smcg, a cosmetic glass container company. SPAC is a company established for a special purpose: to facilitate the letter. SPAC allows companies to raise funds through an initial public offering (IPO) and then merge with high-quality non-listed companies within three years, effectively bypassing the listing process.

The 6th SPAC had its merger shareholder general meeting approve the agenda on March 3rd. It will have a merger date on February 10th and new shares will be listed on March 4th. The 7th SPAC is scheduled to hold a merger shareholder general meeting on February 15th. If the agenda is approved, the merger date will be February 18th, and new shares will be listed on March 1 7th. The 8th SPAC is targeting listing by the end of the year, with plans to merge with Jison, a wireless security company. Currently, the stock exchange review is underway, and the result is expected to be announced within the first quarter.

Under the command of the newly appointed President Moon Joo-seung in 2024, Kiwoom Securities' IB Business Department operating profit has recorded 1,320 billion won by the end of September 2024, significantly growing compared to 548 billion won in 2022 and 224 billion won in 2023. However, the revenue from the ECM (Equity Capital Markets) sector, which includes SPAC mergers, was 62 billion won in 2022, 85 billion won in  ChatGPT
